message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "A short proof that link-irregular tournaments exist for every order at least six"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bhattacharjee
    given-names: Deep
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0466-750X"
    affiliation: "Formerly, Electro-Gravitational Space Propulsion Laboratory (EGSPL), Bhubaneswar, Odisha 751030, India"
    email: d.bhattacharjee@erl-forschung.de
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-09
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/creelie/eConjectureLinkIrregular"
keywords:
  - tournament
  - link-irregular digraph
  - vertex-deleted subtournament
  - score sequence
abstract: >-
  A digraph is link-irregular if no two of its vertices have isomorphic links.
  Bastien and Khormali conjectured that a link-irregular tournament on n
  vertices exists if and only if n >= 6, and proved the case n <= 8; Chau
  proved the conjecture in 2026 by substitution into a transitive tournament.
  We give a short different proof, by a construction that adds two vertices
  at a time.
